   "tagline": "An orbital polyrhythm music box. Planets ride concentric orbits whose periods are locked to integer ratios (2:3:4:5…, primes, odds, fibonacci). Every time a planet sweeps past the 12-o'clock meridian it chimes one note of a scale — outer orbits low, inner orbits high. Polyrhythm becomes something you can *watch*: the pattern drifts apart, tangles, and snaps back into a single chord once per cycle.",
